IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `kn-nouns`
IMPORT `kn-ch1`

-- Mishnah Kinnim, CHAPTER 2: birds that fly from one nest to another, and pairing by species.
-- Target compiler: main.  The priest of chapter 2 still asks first (3:1 says so of chapters 1 and 2:
-- "When is this said?  Of a priest who asks").
-- GENERATED from tools/kn-ch2.l4.in by tools/render.py; edit the template.

§ `Kinnim chapter 2`

-- What becomes of the birds after a flight (2:1, 2:4, 2:5).
DECLARE `Outcome of the flight` IS ONE OF
    `take a mate for the bird left behind`
    `the bird that flew is invalid and invalidates one bird where it landed`
    `nothing is lost`
    `the birds in the middle die and the others are offered as the side they are on`
    `all of them die`

§§ `2:1 one bird of an unassigned pair flies away`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:2 | קן סתומה שפרח ממנה גוזל לאויר, או שפרח לבין המתות, או שמת אחד מהן, יקח זוג לשני.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:3 | פרח לבין הקריבות, פסול ופוסל אחד כנגדו, שהגוזל הפורח, פסול ופוסל אחד כנגדו.
-- An unassigned nest from which a young bird flew into the air, or flew among the birds that must die,
-- or one of them died: let him take a mate for the second.  It flew among the birds to be offered: it
-- is invalid, and invalidates one corresponding to it; for the young bird that flies is invalid and
-- invalidates one corresponding to it.
@ref Kinnim 2:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:2-3)
GIVEN where IS A `Where the bird went`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of the flight`
`what follows when a bird of an unassigned pair goes` where MEANS
    CONSIDER where
    WHEN `into the air`                       THEN `take a mate for the bird left behind`
    WHEN `among birds that must die`          THEN `take a mate for the bird left behind`
    WHEN `it died`                            THEN `take a mate for the bird left behind`
    WHEN `among birds that are to be offered` THEN `the bird that flew is invalid and invalidates one bird where it landed`

§§ `2:2 two women with two nests each`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:5 | כיצד? שתי נשים, לזו שתי קנים ולזו שתי קנים, פרח מזו לזו, פוסל אחד בהליכתו.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:6 | חזר, פוסל אחד בחזירתו.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:7 | פרח וחזר, פרח וחזר, לא הפסיד כלום, שאפילו הן מעורבות, אין פחות משתים.
-- How so?  Two women, to this one two nests and to that one two nests.  It flew from this one to that:
-- it invalidates one in its going.  It returned: it invalidates one in its return.  It flew and
-- returned, flew and returned: it lost nothing, for even if they were all mixed, there are not fewer
-- than two.
-- Counted in nests (pairs): four, then three, then two, and never fewer than two.  "Not fewer than two"
-- is the count 1:3 gives for two nests and two nests mixed together, which this rule uses for the floor.
-- Bartenura shows where the losses fall: after the first flight the first woman can offer one pair
-- (three birds) and the second two (five birds); after the return each can offer one.
@ref Kinnim 2:2 (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:5-7)
GIVEN `one-way flights` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`nests still offerable when two women had two nests each` `one-way flights` MEANS
    max (4 MINUS (min `one-way flights` 2))
        ((`the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 2, 2))) DIVIDED BY 2)

§§ `2:3 seven women, a bird flying to the end and back`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:9 | לזו אחת, לזו שתים, לזו שלש, לזו ארבע, לזו חמש, לזו שש, לזו שבע, פרח מן הראשונה לשניה, לשלישית, לרביעית, לחמישית, לשישית, לשביעית, חזר, פוסל אחד בהליכתו ואחד בחזירתו.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:10 | הראשונה והשניה אין להם כלום, השלישית יש לה אחת, הרביעית יש לה שתים, החמישית יש לה שלש, השישית יש לה ארבע, השביעית יש לה שש.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:11 | פרח וחזר, פוסל אחד בהליכתו, ואחד בחזירתו.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:12 | השלישית והרביעית אין להם כלום, החמישית יש לה אחת, הששית יש לה שתים, השביעית יש לה חמש.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:13 | פרח וחזר, פוסל אחד בהליכתו, ואחד בחזירתו, החמישית והששית אין להם כלום, השביעית יש לה ארבע.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:14 | ויש אומרים, השביעית לא הפסידה כלום.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:15 | ואם פרח מבין המתות לכולם, הרי כולם ימותו.
-- To this one one, to this one two, three, four, five, six, seven.  It flew from the first to the
-- second, the third, the fourth, the fifth, the sixth, the seventh, and returned: it invalidates one in
-- its going and one in its return.  The first and second have nothing; the third has one, the fourth
-- two, the fifth three, the sixth four, the seventh six.  It flew and returned: it invalidates one in
-- its going and one in its return: the third and fourth have nothing, the fifth one, the sixth two, the
-- seventh five.  It flew and returned ...: the fifth and sixth have nothing; the seventh has four.  And
-- some say: the seventh lost nothing.  And if one flew from among the birds that must die into all of
-- them, all of them die.
--
-- READING (Bartenura), not the text: a round trip starts at the first nest that still has a pair to
-- offer and goes to the last nest and back.  Every nest the bird leaves loses a pair: the first and the
-- last nest once, each nest between them twice.  A nest with nothing left stays with nothing.  Bartenura
-- asks why a nest loses a pair even where its neighbour's birds will never be offered, and answers that
-- the sages decreed the loss alike for every flight (גזרינן).  The text's three tables are tests in
-- kn-tests.l4, so this reading is checked against them, not the other way round.
@ref Kinnim 2:3 (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:9-13)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the place of the first nest with a pair left` counts MEANS go 1 counts
    WHERE
        go i l MEANS
            CONSIDER l
            WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
            WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN IF c GREATER THAN 0 THEN i ELSE go (i PLUS 1) rest

@ref Kinnim 2:3 (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:9-13)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the nests left after one round trip` counts MEANS
    zipWith lose counts (range 1 (count counts))
    WHERE
        first MEANS `the place of the first nest with a pair left` counts
        last  MEANS count counts
        lose c i MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF c EQUALS 0      THEN 0
                IF i LESS THAN first THEN c
                IF (i EQUALS first) OR (i EQUALS last) THEN max 0 (c MINUS 1)
                OTHERWISE max 0 (c MINUS 2)

-- "And some say: the seventh lost nothing."  Bartenura reads it of the third round trip: by then the
-- nest before the last has nothing, so the birds that left the last nest will never be offered, and the
-- last nest keeps what it had (eleven birds, five pairs).  As a READING: on a round trip after which the
-- nest before the last has nothing, the last nest loses nothing.  Bartenura: the halakha is not as
-- "some say".
@ref Kinnim 2:3, "some say" (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:14)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the nests left after one round trip, as some say` counts MEANS
    IF (at after (n MINUS 2)) EQUALS 0
        THEN concat (LIST (take (n MINUS 1) after), LIST (at counts (n MINUS 1)))
        ELSE after
    WHERE
        after MEANS `the nests left after one round trip` counts
        n     MEANS count counts

@ref Kinnim 2:3 (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:9-14)
GIVEN counts      IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `round trips` IS A NUMBER
      `as some say` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the nests left after round trips` counts `round trips` `as some say` MEANS
    IF `round trips` AT MOST 0
        THEN counts
        ELSE `the nests left after round trips` next (`round trips` MINUS 1) `as some say`
    WHERE
        next MEANS IF `as some say`
                       THEN `the nests left after one round trip, as some say` counts
                       ELSE `the nests left after one round trip` counts

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:15 | ואם פרח מבין המתות לכולם, הרי כולם ימותו.
@ref Kinnim 2:3 (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:15)
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the nests left when a bird from among those that must die flew into every nest` counts MEANS
    map (GIVEN c YIELD 0) counts

§§ `2:4 an unassigned pair and a designated pair`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:17 | קן סתומה וקן מפורשת, פרח מן הסתומה למפורשת, יקח זוג לשני.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:18 | חזר, או שפרח מן המפורשת ראשון, הרי כולן ימותו.
-- An unassigned nest and a designated nest: it flew from the unassigned to the designated: let him
-- take a mate for the second.  It returned, or it flew from the designated first: all of them die.
-- Bartenura: the two birds of the designated nest had already become mixed with each other, so neither
-- can be told for which it was; the three that are mixed die, and the bird left in the unassigned nest
-- takes a mate.
@ref Kinnim 2:4 (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:17-18)
GIVEN what IS A `Flight between an unassigned and a designated pair`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of the flight`
`what follows a flight between an unassigned and a designated pair` what MEANS
    CONSIDER what
    WHEN `one flew from the unassigned pair to the designated pair` THEN `take a mate for the bird left behind`
    WHEN `then one flew back`                                     THEN `all of them die`
    WHEN `the first flight was from the designated pair`            THEN `all of them die`

§§ `2:5 sin offerings on one side, burnt offerings on the other`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:20 | חטאת מכאן ועולה מכאן וסתומה באמצע, פרח מן האמצע לצדדין, אחד הילך ואחד הילך, לא הפסיד כלום, אלא יאמר, "זה שהלך אצל חטאות, חטאת. וזה שהלך אצל עולות, עולה".
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:21 | חזר לאמצע, האמצעיים ימותו, אלו יקרבו חטאות, ואלו יקרבו עולות.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:22 | חזר [ או שפרח ] מן האמצע לצדדין, הרי כולן ימותו.
-- A sin offering here and a burnt offering there and an unassigned pair in the middle.  It flew from
-- the middle to the sides, one this way and one that way: it lost nothing; but let him say, "this one
-- that went to the sin offerings is a sin offering, and this one that went to the burnt offerings is a
-- burnt offering".  It returned to the middle: the ones in the middle die, these are offered as sin
-- offerings and those as burnt offerings.  It returned [or flew] from the middle to the sides: all of
-- them die.
@ref Kinnim 2:5 (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:20-22)
GIVEN what IS A `Flight from the middle`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of the flight`
`what follows a flight from the middle` what MEANS
    CONSIDER what
    WHEN `one flew from the middle to each side`   THEN `nothing is lost`
    WHEN `those two flew back to the middle`       THEN `the birds in the middle die and the others are offered as the side they are on`
    WHEN `then one flew from the middle to a side` THEN `all of them die`

§§ `2:5 turtledoves and young pigeons`

-- What a woman whose pair was brought of two species must bring again.
DECLARE `What she must bring again` IS ONE OF
    `nothing more`
    `bring again` HAS
        `the offering`    IS AN `Offering`
        `of the species`  IS A `Species`

-- The two views on which offering sets the species.
DECLARE `Reading of 2:5` IS ONE OF
    `the first view`
    `Ben Azzai`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:23 | אין מביאין תורין כנגד בני יונה, ולא בני יונה כנגד תורין.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:24 | כיצד, האשה שהביאה חטאתה תור, ועולתה בן יונה, תכפול ותביא עולתה תור.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:25 | עולתה תור, וחטאתה בן יונה, תכפול ותביא עולתה בן יונה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:26 | בן עזאי אומר, הולכין אחר הראשון.
-- One does not bring turtledoves against young pigeons, nor young pigeons against turtledoves.  How?
-- A woman who brought her sin offering a turtledove and her burnt offering a young pigeon: she doubles,
-- and brings her burnt offering a turtledove.  Her burnt offering a turtledove and her sin offering a
-- young pigeon: she doubles, and brings her burnt offering a young pigeon.  Ben Azzai says: one goes by
-- the first.
-- The first view: the sin offering sets the species, whichever was brought first (Bartenura: "the sin
-- offering is the main one").  Ben Azzai: whichever was brought first sets it, and the other is brought
-- again.  Bartenura: the halakha follows the first view.
@ref Kinnim 2:5 (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:23-26)
GIVEN `species of her sin offering`   IS A `Species`
      `species of her burnt offering` IS A `Species`
      `the sin offering came first`   IS A BOOLEAN
      reading                         IS A `Reading of 2:5`
GIVETH A `What she must bring again`
`what she must bring again when her pair was of two species` `species of her sin offering` `species of her burnt offering` `the sin offering came first` reading MEANS
    IF `species of her sin offering` EQUALS `species of her burnt offering`
        THEN `nothing more`
        ELSE CONSIDER reading
             WHEN `the first view` THEN `bring again` `burnt offering` `species of her sin offering`
             WHEN `Ben Azzai` THEN
                 IF `the sin offering came first`
                     THEN `bring again` `burnt offering` `species of her sin offering`
                     ELSE `bring again` `sin offering` `species of her burnt offering`

§§ `2:5 when she dies`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:27 | האשה שהביאה חטאתה ומתה, יביאו היורשין עולתה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-2:28 | עולתה ומתה, לא יביאו היורשין חטאתה.
-- A woman who brought her sin offering and died: let the heirs bring her burnt offering.  Her burnt
-- offering, and died: the heirs do not bring her sin offering.
-- Bartenura: a sin offering whose owner has died is not offered.
@ref Kinnim 2:5 (src:mishnah-kinnim-2:27-28)
GIVEN `the offering she brought before she died` IS AN `Offering`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`her heirs must bring the other offering of her pair` `the offering she brought before she died` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offering she brought before she died`
    WHEN `sin offering`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `burnt offering` THEN FALSE
